{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -i 'review.*dispatch|delegat|subreaper|abandon|review.*process' .pose/knowledge\"","aggregated_output":".pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-agency-readiness-outcome-review.md:59:ownership exclusions are sandbox limitations, not passed delegation tests.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:3:slug: delegation-mcp-round5\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:10:  spec: pose-delegation-mcp\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:13:    - pose review verify spec:pose-delegation-mcp\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:14:    - pose delegate ls --json\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:19:# Handoff: delegation MCP review residual risks\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:23:Independent round 5 reviewed implementation f0514d01404e7bed0cfc602f2db065f3e0c6289e of spec pose-delegation-mcp. The maintainer-authorized reviewer agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review declares Codex/OpenAI, another vendor than implementer Claude/Anthropic. Identity is declared; this instance uses unsigned attestations. Last reviewed: 2026-10-27. Native global strict validation passed 158/158 checks at that implementation head.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:33:For F02, start or continue a synthetic run through MCP: observe attempt in the immediate response and run in wait. Align the public identity contract or allocate run identity at handback, with regressions for retries. For F03, cancel the invoking process after the active marker is visible and before handback; inspect ls/status, then wait for the same attempt to finish. Document recovery, correlation and checking the ledger before retrying. A transport cancellation is not delegate cancel. Re-review by 2026-11-26 or before changing handback identity/retry behavior.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegation-mcp-round5.md:45:Spec: .pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-mcp.md. Consumed knowledge: knowledge:delegation-observation-round4, knowledge:delegation-routing-round3 and knowledge:delegated-rounds-legacy-status. Canonical validation: .pose/results/delivery-validation.json. Local probes, seven mutations and reports: .review-work/round5/ (deliberately untracked). Native bundle and attestation IDs are recorded in the spec Final Report after closeout.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:3:slug: delegated-rounds-legacy-status\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:10:  spec: pose-delegated-review-round-protocol\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:14:    - pose delegate ls --json\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:23:Independent round 4 of spec pose-delegated-review-round-protocol reviewed fa0c589aac678fe548e3725f745ba6628cef3e8f. All earlier blockers are corrected. Reviewer agent:independent-gpt-6.1-sol-review is the maintainer-authorized declared Codex/OpenAI identity, another vendor than Claude/Anthropic implementation. This instance uses unsigned attestations. Last reviewed on 2026-10-27.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:27:f-r4-01 is low severity: the deprecated pose review status path omits round/thread fields when constructing interrupted summaries in pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_run_continuity.go:611; its text renderer in internal/cli/review_run_continuity.go:116 also omits the round. The current pose delegate ls path and persisted run contain the correct round, and verify/approval do not consume this legacy presentation.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:33:Reproduce with the existing run-continuity fixture or a fake agent that captures a synthetic session and exits with declared limit code 75. Compare the persisted run, pose delegate ls --json, and pose review status --json before resume. Add regression coverage that the legacy summary/text reports the round and relevant lineage, or explicitly document its narrower legacy projection before retirement. Run the continuity, delegation and round suites. Review by 2026-11-26 or before removing the deprecated alias.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:37:Users of the deprecated status command miss round context; the deprecation hint already points to pose delegate ls. This does not turn partial output into a decision, alter the ledger, or bypass approval. Acceptance is limited to this low-severity presentation gap and its existing replacement.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-27-handoff-delegated-rounds-legacy-status.md:45:Spec: .pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-round-protocol.md. Review: .review-work/round4/REPORT.md (local). Native attestation rva-78b867ebfada5dcb on bundle rvb-aaec9b9e16165671 and the spec follow-up record f-r4-01.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:3:slug: delegated-conclusions-round4\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:10:  spec: pose-delegated-review-conclusions\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:14:    - pose review verify spec:pose-delegated-review-conclusions\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:18:# Handoff: delegated conclusion lock diagnostics\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-28-handoff-delegated-conclusions-round4.md:44:Spec: .pose/specs/2026-10-27-pose-delegated-review-conclusions.md. Review report and independent probes: .review-work/round4/report.md. The spec Final Report records the sealed bundle and attestation after closeout. No upstream contribution draft, issue or PR was created.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:3:slug: delegation-observation-round4\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:10:  spec: pose-delegated-review-completion-signal\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:13:    - pose review verify spec:pose-delegated-review-completion-signal\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:21:Independent round 4 of commit a8ce8cf97acb89815cc8440f028ec319c63ec1c3 closes the milestone `observation` of the roadmap `delegation`. The reviewer is the maintainer-authorized declared identity `agent:independent-claude-sonnet-5-5-review` (Claude Sonnet 5.5, Anthropic), the same vendor and another model than the implementer (Claude Opus 5.5, session `f2a4d9f2-d557-4064-ae96-6ed52bb47cd2`); by the rule of 2026-10-09 another model satisfies `different-actor`, another vendor would be preferred. Rounds 1 and 2 were Codex (OpenAI), round 3 and this one Claude Sonnet 5.5. N02 (a detached run read a relative `--note-file` from the project root instead of the caller's directory) and the follow-ups F-R3-01, F-R3-03, F-R3-04, F-R3-06, F-R3-08 and F-R3-10 were reconciled as fixed; no blocker remains.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:28:- F-R3-02 (low, graded medium in round 3 and lowered because the hand-back now precedes the agent, which leaves a window of about 100ms or a supervisor hung over 30s; the engine accepts only low as accepted risk): the SIGTERM, 30s grace and SIGKILL path of a stopped supervisor has no test (swapping SIGTERM for SIGKILL keeps the delegate suites green), and the SIGKILL fallback on the supervisor group does not reach the agent's own group.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:30:- F-R3-07 (low): `on_terminal` fires for `pose delegate review|resume`, not for the deprecated alias `pose review dispatch --via … --apply` nor for a run recorded `stalled`.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:32:- F-R4-01 (low): F-R3-03, F-R3-04, F-R3-08 and F-R3-10 have no regression test; reverting each leaves `Delegat|Watch|Stall|Help|Detach` green. F-R3-04 and F-R3-10 are testable.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:36:- F-R4-05 (low): the regression tests of the review rounds are named outside the `TestDelegat*`/`TestDelegate*` family (`TestADetachedRunReadsTheCallersFiles`, `TestHookBoundAndRelativeCommand`, `TestAnUnrecordedHookOutcomeIsReported`, `TestADetachedRunThatCannotHandBackDoesNotRun`), so the `delegation-surface-integration` check and the documented race selection do not run them; only the unit lane does.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:40:`go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run 'TestADetachedRun|TestHookBound|TestAnUnrecordedHook' -count=1` and the race selection extended with those names. For F-R3-02 a test that holds a supervisor past the grace. For F-R4-01 a stalled-watch test and a test whose live file cannot be read. Run `pose delegate --help` and the four manuals after any change.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:44:None of these changes dispatch, ledger, continuity, provenance or containment; each is either a disclosure gap, a test gap or a window of at most six minutes. F-R3-05 and F-R3-02 can leave an agent running after its supervisor died; the stalled state and `ls` name the run, and `pose delegate cancel` stops one that is still recorded.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:52:Spec: `.pose/specs/2026-10-18-pose-delegated-review-completion-signal.md`. ADR: `.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md`. Roadmap: `.pose/roadmaps/delegation.md`. Review report: `.review-work/round4/REPORT.md` (local evidence only).\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-routing-round3.md:3:slug: delegation-routing-round3\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-routing-round3.md:10:  spec: pose-delegation-routing\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-routing-round3.md:13:    - pose review verify spec:pose-delegation-routing\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-routing-round3.md:25:F08: internal/cli/delegate.go computes independent_of_lead using vendor inequality alone. Configure a schema-2 agent with vendor unknown, model unknown, cli sh and read command [sh]. Both `pose delegate agents --lead anthropic/opus --json` and its text form disclose independent_of_lead=true. The correct conservative result is false or explicitly unknown. The auto router, achieved independence and run-backed authority do not consume this boolean. Acceptance is limited to this disclosure defect, not permission to credit unknown identities with independence.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-routing-round3.md:27:F09: internal/pose/delegation_policy.go uses omitempty for routing.on_unavailable. Parse a valid policy whose only agent matches anthropic/opus and whose routing.on_unavailable is []; auto refuses it. Pass that policy through CanonicalDelegationPolicy and ParseDelegationPolicy again; the list disappears and the default same-model fallback selects the agent. The existing production canonical writer only converts schema 1, which has no such routing list, or prints examples; it does not rewrite existing schema-2 policy. Acceptance is limited to that currently unconsumed serialization path. Do not add a schema-2 policy writer without addressing it; declared agent order must also survive any future serializer used for existing policy.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-routing-round3.md:35:F08 may mislead a user choosing an agent, but does not establish a run proof or approval. F09 would enable fallbacks a caller explicitly disabled if a future writer used the helper on existing schema-2 policy. Neither requires changing the execution, ledger, containment or provenance contracts. R10 remains a shared detector delivery; actual task invocation belongs to pose-delegation-task and is not represented as executed here.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-routing-round3.md:43:Spec: `.pose/specs/2026-10-26-pose-delegation-routing.md`. ADR: `.pose/adr/2026-10-26-delegation-is-a-first-class-execution-surface.md`. Review report: `.review-work/round3/REPORT.md` (local evidence only).\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-04-handoff-pose-b34-implementation.md:112:@pose-maintainers. A coordenação mantém integração e gates. Use `pose delegate`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
