{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_79","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"diff -u POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md | sed -n '1,180p'\"","aggregated_output":"--- POSE.md\t2026-11-24 23:08:09.615993425 -0300\n+++ pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\t2026-11-24 23:08:09.655834963 -0300\n@@ -574,19 +574,6 @@\n - assisted execution via [`pose`](pose) (CLI)\n - progressive maturity with skills in [`.agents/skills/`](.agents/skills/)\n \n-## Open-Source POSE Contributor Mode\n-\n-<!-- pose:contributor-mode -->\n-\n-This repository has enabled POSE Contributor Mode. Executing AI agents collaborate on improving POSE engine stability and developer experience under explicit user adjudication.\n-\n-- **Continuous Opportunity Scouting**: On every issue resolution or task execution, proactively scout for related improvements, edge cases, root-level parity gaps, or complementary corrections across adjacent tools and commands.\n-- **User Consent & Explicit Adjudication**: Staging or submitting contributions upstream is ALWAYS an explicit user decision. Agents must ask the user for confirmation before staging drafts under `.pose/contributions/` or opening GitHub issues.\n-- **Lifecycle & Status Integrity**: Track contribution states (`staged` -> `submitted` / `dismissed`) with `pose contribute list --status <staged|submitted|dismissed|all>`, `pose contribute submit <file>`, `pose contribute mark-submitted <file> [--issue-url <url>]`, or `pose contribute dismiss <file>`.\n-- Check contributor status: `pose contribute status`\n-- Stage a contribution manually: `pose contribute stage --type <bug|enhancement> --title <title>`\n-- Disable contributor mode: `pose contribute disable`\n-- Privacy guarantee: staged reports strictly isolate POSE engine mechanics and never leak proprietary code.\n ## Opt-in progressive review profiles (ABM)\n \n Add `engineering-judgment@1` and/or `high-criticality-review@1` explicitly to\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"agent_message","text":"The English scaffold difference is only the repository-specific Contributor Mode section, which the scaffold intentionally omits; the new process paragraph matches in both copies, and the PT-BR files are identical. The remaining findings are the Windows no-op cleanup path and two inaccuracies in the bounded termination report. I’m assembling the complete draft now and will run it through the required preflight."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_81","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'POSE_REVIEW_DRAFT' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\nIndependent review of `spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes`\n\ndecision: changes-requested\n\nFindings:\n\n- **N1 — medium, blocker** — [pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4083797052/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go:8). The non-Linux fallback says process-group termination is available, but Windows implements both process-group functions as no-ops ([review_dispatch_windows.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4083797052/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_windows.go:14)). A Windows review can leave a child alive while dispatch continues into worktree checks and cleanup. The manuals repeat this inaccurate platform claim.\n- **N2 — low, follow-up** — [pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4083797052/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:167). A PID is recorded as ended when SIGKILL delivery succeeds, before the reaper confirms it exited. If it remains alive past the bound, the run record still lists it as ended alongside a generic incomplete-reap error.\n- **N3 — low, follow-up** — [pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4083797052/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1130). When more than 1,001 PIDs are reported, the dispatch uses the capped PID list plus a single “and N more” entry to calculate the headline count, so it reports 1,001 regardless of the larger total.\n\nValidation: the focused tests, focused race tests, the adapter exit-status test, and focused `go vet` passed. Both strict validate commands were attempted but failed before Go checks because the read-only sandbox denied Go temporary build/cache writes; sealed build, e2e, integration and unit evidence is used for those tools. `surface-check` passed with 0 findings. `artifact-check` exited 0 but resolved change set `cs-06c6af066283` (head `3994f49`), rather than the brief’s `cs-cd7b2a0ff10a`, and emitted 988 orphan warnings, so I did not treat it as scoped attribution evidence. Tech-debt assessment was incomplete due to two unrelated invalid specs and an uncovered panic in `bounded_cache.go`. Closeout and review checks are deferred because they require an attestation, which this task forbids.\n\nThe sweep covered the Linux shim/reaper and fallback paths, dispatch/report lifecycle, attempt release and ledger flow, CLI/help contract, review-brief template, English and PT-BR manuals and scaffold copies, and the associated regression tests. Rules applied: `.pose/workflows/review.md`, `.pose/rules/backend-go.md`, `.pose/rules/security.md`, and `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`. No repository changes or attestations were made.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go\",\n      \"line\": 8,\n      \"summary\": \"The non-Linux fallback and manuals claim process-group termination, but the Windows build'\"'s isolateProcessGroup and killProcessGroup are no-ops (review_dispatch_windows.go:14-16). A reviewer child can survive while dispatch proceeds to worktree checks and cleanup, so R1 is not met on Windows. Qualify Windows as unsupported and fail closed, or implement safe process-tree termination.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 167,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The shim records a PID as ended after SIGKILL delivery but before confirming it was reaped. If the child remains through the reaping deadline, the failed run still says it ended while reporting only a generic residual count.\\\",\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Distinguish signalled PIDs from PIDs verified reaped, and record per-PID residual state on timeout.\\\",\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"pose-mcp maintainers\\\",\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-24\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 1130,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"When the shim reports more than 1,001 PIDs, the dispatch reports len(reaped), which counts the 1,000 listed PIDs plus one summary placeholder instead of the actual EndedTotal.\\\",\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Use EndedTotal for the bounded shim report's headline count and cover a report above 1,001 PIDs.\\\",\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"pose-mcp maintainers\\\",\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-24\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R10-N3\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:165-169,182-184: the PID is now appended only after SIGKILL delivery succeeds and the dispatcher records the shim error, but the PID is still labelled ended before the child is confirmed reaped.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R11-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:976-991: on Linux, executable or pipe setup failure returns a failed run instead of launching without the shim.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R11-N2\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:220-240 and review_reap_linux_test.go:233-249: ESRCH returns delivered=false; the regression test verifies an already-ended child is not reported as ended.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R11-N3\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go:1147-1154: the cancel output reports the actual status of a run already recorded for the attempt.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept the scoped Linux shim/reaper and non-Linux fallback, dispatch setup/report/cleanup, reservation/receipt/marker release paths, delegate ls/cancel/help, review-brief/10 rendering and digest, English and PT-BR manuals and embedded scaffold copies, and related regression tests. The shim's Linux process scan is limited to its own children and uses pidfd pinning; it cannot signal the dispatcher or a sibling run. Identified N1-N3; no repository changes or attestation were made.\\\",\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-379f57a5ed0682c0\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"I examined the Linux CLI shim enablement in cmd/pose/main.go, the shim child scan and pidfd checks, and the design assessment's empty delta list. Linux dispatch uses its isolated shim; the non-shim embedder fallback remains reviewer-settable under L6; L1-L4 are explicit residuals. Windows has no process-group implementation, which I recorded as N1 rather than treating the L2 assumption as verified.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Linux process ownership and release serialization passed focused unit and race checks, but Windows has no child termination path and can continue cleanup with a live reviewer child.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The change adds the --confirm-abandoned cancel flag and status output while preserving schema-1 run/receipt records. The new cancel CLI branch is a known gap in the spec; I inspected the branch and the store-level release tests, while existing CLI integration evidence covers the delegation surface.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The release refuses live owners, unreadable markers, incomplete run history, and unconfirmed markerless reservations with bounded errors; the full sealed unit evidence and focused release tests cover these paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The changed boundary is the pose-mcp CLI/domain ledger; no HTTP, protobuf, Kafka, or MCP tool contract changed. The integration assessment's three unobserved HTTP routes are unrelated to this scope.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The failed cleanup path can label a signalled but unreaped PID as ended. N3 also makes the bounded report's headline count inaccurate above 1,001 processes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The CLI change is additive, existing record schemas remain unchanged, and the localized command help documents the new confirmation flag.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Linux dispatch reaps the shim subtree before inventory, but Windows builds no-op the process-group functions and can finish inventory with a reviewer child still alive.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-379f57a5ed0682c0\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses the cause of escaped reviewer commands by placing subreaper authority in a single run shim, avoiding dispatcher-wide adoption; D2 closes abandoned attempts through a failed run and receipt. Process-group-only and environment-only cleanup are insufficient for Linux reviewers that setsid or clear their environment. The structural assessment reported no delta facts requiring mapping.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The new fallback comment and manuals claim process-group termination on other platforms, while Windows implements neither process groups nor a kill operation.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The cancel recovery path provides the cause and release command, but an incomplete shim reaping can leave a contradictory ended-PID statement in the failed run record.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R1's process cleanup is not provided on Windows; N2 also falls short of R2's accurate list of terminated processes in the unreaped-child failure case.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-379f57a5ed0682c0\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The subject changes implement R1-R6, D1-D2 and the paired documentation/template updates; the Linux shim, platform fallback and attempt-release additions stay within the approved pose-mcp surface.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"On Linux the shim scan cannot signal the dispatcher or sibling runs, and the fd-3 report closes on exec. On Windows a surviving reviewer child can retain any explicitly authorized environment credential after the run.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-379f57a5ed0682c0\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The per-run shim is the smallest boundary that handles setsid/environment-clearing descendants without process-wide subreaper effects; pidfds prevent PID-reuse signalling. It adds no cgroup or service-manager controls, so L1 remains the invalidating condition. The Windows fallback mismatch is separately recorded as N1.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The command exited 0, but resolved cs-06c6af066283 at head 3994f49 rather than the brief'\"'s cs-cd7b2a0ff10a and emitted 988 orphan warnings. I report this scope mismatch and rely on the supplied sealed subject list for the reviewed paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-379f57a5ed0682c0\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The required design assessment ran successfully and observed no structural deltas.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completed successfully and discovered pose-mcp; no assessment state was persisted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The assessment command completed but reported three unobserved existing HTTP consumers (/admin/refresh, /healthz, /mcp), none of which changed in this scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The scan was incomplete because two unrelated specs have invalid follow-up bullets; it also reported an uncovered panic at pose-mcp/internal/pose/bounded_cache.go:334, outside the reviewed subject.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI closeout-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred because this completion check requires the review conclusion to be recorded, which the brief forbids.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI review-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred because this completion check requires the review conclusion to be recorded, which the brief forbids.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Selected the review workflow, backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The required surface check ran successfully: one delivery target, 236 results, zero findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The global strict validation was attempted but every Go check failed before compilation because the read-only sandbox denied temporary build/cache writes. The sealed unit evidence and all listed build, e2e and integration evidence pass; focused tests, race tests, the adapter exit-status test and focused vet also passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The module strict validation was attempted but could not start Go checks because the read-only sandbox denied build/cache writes. The sealed pose-mcp unit evidence passes; focused tests, race tests, the adapter exit-status test and focused vet passed in this run.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\nPOSE_REVIEW_DRAFT'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_81","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'POSE_REVIEW_DRAFT' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\nIndependent review of `spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes`\n\ndecision: changes-requested\n\nFindings:\n\n- **N1 — medium, blocker** — [pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4083797052/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go:8). The non-Linux fallback says process-group termination is available, but Windows implements both process-group functions as no-ops ([review_dispatch_windows.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4083797052/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_windows.go:14)). A Windows review can leave a child alive while dispatch continues into worktree checks and cleanup. The manuals repeat this inaccurate platform claim.\n- **N2 — low, follow-up** — [pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4083797052/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:167). A PID is recorded as ended when SIGKILL delivery succeeds, before the reaper confirms it exited. If it remains alive past the bound, the run record still lists it as ended alongside a generic incomplete-reap error.\n- **N3 — low, follow-up** — [pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4083797052/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1130). When more than 1,001 PIDs are reported, the dispatch uses the capped PID list plus a single “and N more” entry to calculate the headline count, so it reports 1,001 regardless of the larger total.\n\nValidation: the focused tests, focused race tests, the adapter exit-status test, and focused `go vet` passed. Both strict validate commands were attempted but failed before Go checks because the read-only sandbox denied Go temporary build/cache writes; sealed build, e2e, integration and unit evidence is used for those tools. `surface-check` passed with 0 findings. `artifact-check` exited 0 but resolved change set `cs-06c6af066283` (head `3994f49`), rather than the brief’s `cs-cd7b2a0ff10a`, and emitted 988 orphan warnings, so I did not treat it as scoped attribution evidence. Tech-debt assessment was incomplete due to two unrelated invalid specs and an uncovered panic in `bounded_cache.go`. Closeout and review checks are deferred because they require an attestation, which this task forbids.\n\nThe sweep covered the Linux shim/reaper and fallback paths, dispatch/report lifecycle, attempt release and ledger flow, CLI/help contract, review-brief template, English and PT-BR manuals and scaffold copies, and the associated regression tests. Rules applied: `.pose/workflows/review.md`, `.pose/rules/backend-go.md`, `.pose/rules/security.md`, and `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`. No repository changes or attestations were made.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go\",\n      \"line\": 8,\n      \"summary\": \"The non-Linux fallback and manuals claim process-group termination, but the Windows build'\"'s isolateProcessGroup and killProcessGroup are no-ops (review_dispatch_windows.go:14-16). A reviewer child can survive while dispatch proceeds to worktree checks and cleanup, so R1 is not met on Windows. Qualify Windows as unsupported and fail closed, or implement safe process-tree termination.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 167,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The shim records a PID as ended after SIGKILL delivery but before confirming it was reaped. If the child remains through the reaping deadline, the failed run still says it ended while reporting only a generic residual count.\\\",\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Distinguish signalled PIDs from PIDs verified reaped, and record per-PID residual state on timeout.\\\",\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"pose-mcp maintainers\\\",\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-24\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 1130,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"When the shim reports more than 1,001 PIDs, the dispatch reports len(reaped), which counts the 1,000 listed PIDs plus one summary placeholder instead of the actual EndedTotal.\\\",\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Use EndedTotal for the bounded shim report's headline count and cover a report above 1,001 PIDs.\\\",\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"pose-mcp maintainers\\\",\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-24\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R10-N3\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:165-169,182-184: the PID is now appended only after SIGKILL delivery succeeds and the dispatcher records the shim error, but the PID is still labelled ended before the child is confirmed reaped.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R11-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:976-991: on Linux, executable or pipe setup failure returns a failed run instead of launching without the shim.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R11-N2\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:220-240 and review_reap_linux_test.go:233-249: ESRCH returns delivered=false; the regression test verifies an already-ended child is not reported as ended.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R11-N3\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go:1147-1154: the cancel output reports the actual status of a run already recorded for the attempt.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept the scoped Linux shim/reaper and non-Linux fallback, dispatch setup/report/cleanup, reservation/receipt/marker release paths, delegate ls/cancel/help, review-brief/10 rendering and digest, English and PT-BR manuals and embedded scaffold copies, and related regression tests. The shim's Linux process scan is limited to its own children and uses pidfd pinning; it cannot signal the dispatcher or a sibling run. Identified N1-N3; no repository changes or attestation were made.\\\",\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-379f57a5ed0682c0\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"I examined the Linux CLI shim enablement in cmd/pose/main.go, the shim child scan and pidfd checks, and the design assessment's empty delta list. Linux dispatch uses its isolated shim; the non-shim embedder fallback remains reviewer-settable under L6; L1-L4 are explicit residuals. Windows has no process-group implementation, which I recorded as N1 rather than treating the L2 assumption as verified.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Linux process ownership and release serialization passed focused unit and race checks, but Windows has no child termination path and can continue cleanup with a live reviewer child.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The change adds the --confirm-abandoned cancel flag and status output while preserving schema-1 run/receipt records. The new cancel CLI branch is a known gap in the spec; I inspected the branch and the store-level release tests, while existing CLI integration evidence covers the delegation surface.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The release refuses live owners, unreadable markers, incomplete run history, and unconfirmed markerless reservations with bounded errors; the full sealed unit evidence and focused release tests cover these paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The changed boundary is the pose-mcp CLI/domain ledger; no HTTP, protobuf, Kafka, or MCP tool contract changed. The integration assessment's three unobserved HTTP routes are unrelated to this scope.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The failed cleanup path can label a signalled but unreaped PID as ended. N3 also makes the bounded report's headline count inaccurate above 1,001 processes.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The CLI change is additive, existing record schemas remain unchanged, and the localized command help documents the new confirmation flag.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Linux dispatch reaps the shim subtree before inventory, but Windows builds no-op the process-group functions and can finish inventory with a reviewer child still alive.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-379f57a5ed0682c0\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses the cause of escaped reviewer commands by placing subreaper authority in a single run shim, avoiding dispatcher-wide adoption; D2 closes abandoned attempts through a failed run and receipt. Process-group-only and environment-only cleanup are insufficient for Linux reviewers that setsid or clear their environment. The structural assessment reported no delta facts requiring mapping.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The new fallback comment and manuals claim process-group termination on other platforms, while Windows implements neither process groups nor a kill operation.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The cancel recovery path provides the cause and release command, but an incomplete shim reaping can leave a contradictory ended-PID statement in the failed run record.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R1's process cleanup is not provided on Windows; N2 also falls short of R2's accurate list of terminated processes in the unreaped-child failure case.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-379f57a5ed0682c0\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The subject changes implement R1-R6, D1-D2 and the paired documentation/template updates; the Linux shim, platform fallback and attempt-release additions stay within the approved pose-mcp surface.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"On Linux the shim scan cannot signal the dispatcher or sibling runs, and the fd-3 report closes on exec. On Windows a surviving reviewer child can retain any explicitly authorized environment credential after the run.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-379f57a5ed0682c0\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The per-run shim is the smallest boundary that handles setsid/environment-clearing descendants without process-wide subreaper effects; pidfds prevent PID-reuse signalling. It adds no cgroup or service-manager controls, so L1 remains the invalidating condition. The Windows fallback mismatch is separately recorded as N1.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The command exited 0, but resolved cs-06c6af066283 at head 3994f49 rather than the brief'\"'s cs-cd7b2a0ff10a and emitted 988 orphan warnings. I report this scope mismatch and rely on the supplied sealed subject list for the reviewed paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-379f57a5ed0682c0\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The required design assessment ran successfully and observed no structural deltas.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completed successfully and discovered pose-mcp; no assessment state was persisted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The assessment command completed but reported three unobserved existing HTTP consumers (/admin/refresh, /healthz, /mcp), none of which changed in this scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The scan was incomplete because two unrelated specs have invalid follow-up bullets; it also reported an uncovered panic at pose-mcp/internal/pose/bounded_cache.go:334, outside the reviewed subject.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI closeout-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred because this completion check requires the review conclusion to be recorded, which the brief forbids.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI review-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred because this completion check requires the review conclusion to be recorded, which the brief forbids.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Selected the review workflow, backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The required surface check ran successfully: one delivery target, 236 results, zero findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The global strict validation was attempted but every Go check failed before compilation because the read-only sandbox denied temporary build/cache writes. The sealed unit evidence and all listed build, e2e and integration evidence pass; focused tests, race tests, the adapter exit-status test and focused vet also passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The module strict validation was attempted but could not start Go checks because the read-only sandbox denied build/cache writes. The sealed pose-mcp unit evidence passes; focused tests, race tests, the adapter exit-status test and focused vet passed in this run.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\nPOSE_REVIEW_DRAFT'","aggregated_output":"Draft check: the conclusion step would accept this draft.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_82","type":"agent_message","text":"Independent review of `spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes`\n\ndecision: changes-requested\n\nFindings:\n\n- **N1 — medium, blocker** — [pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4083797052/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go:8). The non-Linux fallback says process-group termination is available, but Windows implements both process-group functions as no-ops ([review_dispatch_windows.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4083797052/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_windows.go:14)). A Windows review can leave a child alive while dispatch continues into worktree checks and cleanup. The manuals repeat this inaccurate platform claim.\n- **N2 — low, follow-up** — [pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4083797052/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:167). A PID is recorded as ended when SIGKILL delivery succeeds, before the reaper confirms it exited. If it remains alive past the bound, the run record still lists it as ended alongside a generic incomplete-reap error.\n- **N3 — low, follow-up** — [pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4083797052/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1130). When more than 1,001 PIDs are reported, the dispatch uses the capped PID list plus a single “and N more” entry to calculate the headline count, so it reports 1,001 regardless of the larger total.\n\nValidation: the focused tests, focused race tests, the adapter exit-status test, and focused `go vet` passed. Both strict validate commands were attempted but failed before Go checks because the read-only sandbox denied Go temporary build/cache writes; sealed build, e2e, integration and unit evidence is used for those tools. `surface-check` passed with 0 findings. `artifact-check` exited 0 but resolved change set `cs-06c6af066283` (head `3994f49`), rather than the brief’s `cs-cd7b2a0ff10a`, and emitted 988 orphan warnings, so I did not treat it as scoped attribution evidence. Tech-debt assessment was incomplete due to two unrelated invalid specs and an uncovered panic in `bounded_cache.go`. Closeout and review checks are deferred because they require an attestation, which this task forbids.\n\nThe sweep covered the Linux shim/reaper and fallback paths, dispatch/report lifecycle, attempt release and ledger flow, CLI/help contract, review-brief template, English and PT-BR manuals and scaffold copies, and the associated regression tests. Rules applied: `.pose/workflows/review.md`, `.pose/rules/backend-go.md`, `.pose/rules/security.md`, and `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`. No repository changes or attestations were made.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go\",\n      \"line\": 8,\n      \"summary\": \"The non-Linux fallback and manuals claim process-group termination, but the Windows build's isolateProcessGroup and killProcessGroup are no-ops (review_dispatch_windows.go:14-16). A reviewer child can survive while dispatch proceeds to worktree checks and cleanup, so R1 is not met on Windows. Qualify Windows as unsupported and fail closed, or implement safe process-tree termination.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go\",\n      \"line\": 167,\n      \"summary\": \"The shim records a PID as ended after SIGKILL delivery but before confirming it was reaped. If the child remains through the reaping deadline, the failed run still says it ended while reporting only a generic residual count.\",\n      \"action\": \"Distinguish signalled PIDs from PIDs verified reaped, and record per-PID residual state on timeout.\",\n      \"owner\": \"pose-mcp maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-24\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N3\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\n      \"line\": 1130,\n      \"summary\": \"When the shim reports more than 1,001 PIDs, the dispatch reports len(reaped), which counts the 1,000 listed PIDs plus one summary placeholder instead of the actual EndedTotal.\",\n      \"action\": \"Use EndedTotal for the bounded shim report's headline count and cover a report above 1,001 PIDs.\",\n      \"owner\": \"pose-mcp maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-24\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R10-N3\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:165-169,182-184: the PID is now appended only after SIGKILL delivery succeeds and the dispatcher records the shim error, but the PID is still labelled ended before the child is confirmed reaped.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R11-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:976-991: on Linux, executable or pipe setup failure returns a failed run instead of launching without the shim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R11-N2\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:220-240 and review_reap_linux_test.go:233-249: ESRCH returns delivered=false; the regression test verifies an already-ended child is not reported as ended.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R11-N3\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go:1147-1154: the cancel output reports the actual status of a run already recorded for the attempt.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Swept the scoped Linux shim/reaper and non-Linux fallback, dispatch setup/report/cleanup, reservation/receipt/marker release paths, delegate ls/cancel/help, review-brief/10 rendering and digest, English and PT-BR manuals and embedded scaffold copies, and related regression tests. The shim's Linux process scan is limited to its own children and uses pidfd pinning; it cannot signal the dispatcher or a sibling run. Identified N1-N3; no repository changes or attestation were made.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-379f57a5ed0682c0\",\n      \"rationale\": \"I examined the Linux CLI shim enablement in cmd/pose/main.go, the shim child scan and pidfd checks, and the design assessment's empty delta list. Linux dispatch uses its isolated shim; the non-shim embedder fallback remains reviewer-settable under L6; L1-L4 are explicit residuals. Windows has no process-group implementation, which I recorded as N1 rather than treating the L2 assumption as verified.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Linux process ownership and release serialization passed focused unit and race checks, but Windows has no child termination path and can continue cleanup with a live reviewer child.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The change adds the --confirm-abandoned cancel flag and status output while preserving schema-1 run/receipt records. The new cancel CLI branch is a known gap in the spec; I inspected the branch and the store-level release tests, while existing CLI integration evidence covers the delegation surface.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The release refuses live owners, unreadable markers, incomplete run history, and unconfirmed markerless reservations with bounded errors; the full sealed unit evidence and focused release tests cover these paths.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The changed boundary is the pose-mcp CLI/domain ledger; no HTTP, protobuf, Kafka, or MCP tool contract changed. The integration assessment's three unobserved HTTP routes are unrelated to this scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The failed cleanup path can label a signalled but unreaped PID as ended. N3 also makes the bounded report's headline count inaccurate above 1,001 processes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The CLI change is additive, existing record schemas remain unchanged, and the localized command help documents the new confirmation flag.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Linux dispatch reaps the shim subtree before inventory, but Windows builds no-op the process-group functions and can finish inventory with a reviewer child still alive.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-379f57a5ed0682c0\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 addresses the cause of escaped reviewer commands by placing subreaper authority in a single run shim, avoiding dispatcher-wide adoption; D2 closes abandoned attempts through a failed run and receipt. Process-group-only and environment-only cleanup are insufficient for Linux reviewers that setsid or clear their environment. The structural assessment reported no delta facts requiring mapping.\",\n      \"mappings\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The new fallback comment and manuals claim process-group termination on other platforms, while Windows implements neither process groups nor a kill operation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The cancel recovery path provides the cause and release command, but an incomplete shim reaping can leave a contradictory ended-PID statement in the failed run record.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1's process cleanup is not provided on Windows; N2 also falls short of R2's accurate list of terminated processes in the unreaped-child failure case.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-379f57a5ed0682c0\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The subject changes implement R1-R6, D1-D2 and the paired documentation/template updates; the Linux shim, platform fallback and attempt-release additions stay within the approved pose-mcp surface.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"On Linux the shim scan cannot signal the dispatcher or sibling runs, and the fd-3 report closes on exec. On Windows a surviving reviewer child can retain any explicitly authorized environment credential after the run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-379f57a5ed0682c0\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The per-run shim is the smallest boundary that handles setsid/environment-clearing descendants without process-wide subreaper effects; pidfds prevent PID-reuse signalling. It adds no cgroup or service-manager controls, so L1 remains the invalidating condition. The Windows fallback mismatch is separately recorded as N1.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The command exited 0, but resolved cs-06c6af066283 at head 3994f49 rather than the brief's cs-cd7b2a0ff10a and emitted 988 orphan warnings. I report this scope mismatch and rely on the supplied sealed subject list for the reviewed paths.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-379f57a5ed0682c0\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The required design assessment ran successfully and observed no structural deltas.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completed successfully and discovered pose-mcp; no assessment state was persisted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The assessment command completed but reported three unobserved existing HTTP consumers (/admin/refresh, /healthz, /mcp), none of which changed in this scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The scan was incomplete because two unrelated specs have invalid follow-up bullets; it also reported an uncovered panic at pose-mcp/internal/pose/bounded_cache.go:334, outside the reviewed subject.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI closeout-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred because this completion check requires the review conclusion to be recorded, which the brief forbids.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI review-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred because this completion check requires the review conclusion to be recorded, which the brief forbids.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:$POSE_REVIEW_CLI suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Selected the review workflow, backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The required surface check ran successfully: one delivery target, 236 results, zero findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The global strict validation was attempted but every Go check failed before compilation because the read-only sandbox denied temporary build/cache writes. The sealed unit evidence and all listed build, e2e and integration evidence pass; focused tests, race tests, the adapter exit-status test and focused vet also passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The module strict validation was attempted but could not start Go checks because the read-only sandbox denied build/cache writes. The sealed pose-mcp unit evidence passes; focused tests, race tests, the adapter exit-status test and focused vet passed in this run.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
